     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet, because the total daily dose looks too high.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times a day comes to **5100 mg of metformin per day**. The maximum labeled dose for adults is **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times a day, and 2000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about twice that limit. The risks include lactic acidosis and severe GI side effects, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **Metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the labeled max for immediate-release)\n2. **Metformin 1700 mg/day total**, split into doses, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n3. Something else, such as an extended-release form or a different strength\n\nTell me which one is right and I'll enter it. If you really do intend 1700 mg three times a day, confirm that and give a brief clinical reason. I'll add your reason as a note on the order so pharmacy can see it when they review."
      }
     ],
